{"assets":["/statement-assets/be503f76754fbe291b6353b16ebfa05ea3d88db7e8c4efea2a7b0727ecf1f996.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1775","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Interesting Sequence"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Petya and his friend, robot Petya++, like to solve exciting math problems."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One day Petya++ came up with the numbers $$$n$$$ and $$$x$$$ and wrote the following equality on the board: $$$$$$n\\ \\&\\ (n+1)\\ \\&\\ \\dots\\ \\&\\ m = x,$$$$$$ where $$$\\&$$$ denotes the "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bitwise_operation#AND"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise AND operation"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then he suggested his friend Petya find such a minimal $$$m$$$ ($$$m \\ge n$$$) that the equality on the board holds."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Unfortunately, Petya couldn't solve this problem in his head and decided to ask for computer help. He quickly wrote a program and found the answer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Can you solve this difficult problem?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/be503f76754fbe291b6353b16ebfa05ea3d88db7e8c4efea2a7b0727ecf1f996.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 2000$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains two integers $$$n$$$, $$$x$$$ ($$$0\\le n, x \\le 10^{18}$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For every test case, output the smallest possible value of $$$m$$$ such that equality holds."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the equality does not hold for any $$$m$$$, print $$$-1$$$ instead."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can show that if the required $$$m$$$ exists, it does not exceed $$$5 \\cdot 10^{18}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n10 8\n10 10\n10 42\n20 16\n1000000000000000000 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n12\n10\n-1\n24\n1152921504606846976\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, $$$10\\ \\&\\ 11 = 10$$$, but $$$10\\ \\&\\ 11\\ \\&\\ 12 = 8$$$, so the answer is $$$12$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, $$$10 = 10$$$, so the answer is $$$10$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third example, we can see that the required $$$m$$$ does not exist, so we have to print $$$-1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1775C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1775/problem/C"}